Files: cargo-vendor/*
Copyright: respective crate authors
License: Apache-2.0 or MIT or BSD-2-Clause or BSD-3-Clause or ISC or Zlib
 or MPL-2.0 or Unicode-3.0 or Unlicense or CC0-1.0 or MIT-0 or 0BSD or BSL-1.0
Comment:
 Crates vendored by `cargo vendor --locked` for offline Launchpad builds.
 Each crate directory retains its upstream license texts.
 .
 License inventory audited 2026-07-17 from the `license` field of every
 vendored crate manifest (908 unique crate versions, none unlicensed). All
 licenses are permissive or file-level weak copyleft (MPL-2.0: cssparser,
 cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext, pam-client, selectors). Two
 crates offer a copyleft alternative in a disjunction; the permissive
 option is elected for this package: self_cell (Apache-2.0, not
 GPL-2.0-only) and r-efi (MIT, not LGPL-2.1-or-later). A few crates use
 Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception as one arm of a disjunction; plain
 Apache-2.0 is elected.

Files: npm-vendor/*
Copyright: respective npm package authors
License: MIT or Apache-2.0 or ISC or BSD-2-Clause or BSD-3-Clause or Python-2.0
Comment:
 npm package tree for the Tauri log viewer, packed as
 npm-vendor/logs-node_modules.tar.xz. License texts are inside the archive.
 .
 License inventory audited 2026-07-17 from every package.json in the
 archive (234 packages). Python-2.0 covers only `argparse`. Entries
 without a `license` field are test fixtures inside the `resolve`
 package's test suite, covered by resolve's MIT license.

Files: rust-toolchain-dist/*
Copyright: The Rust Project Developers
License: Apache-2.0 or MIT
Comment:
 Prebuilt Rust toolchain (rustc, cargo, standard library) bundled for
 offline Launchpad builds, because Ubuntu's packaged rustc is below this
 tree's MSRV. Upstream: https://www.rust-lang.org (dual MIT/Apache-2.0).
 The toolchain additionally contains LLVM components licensed under
 Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception; the bundled tree retains upstream license
 texts, and rust-toolchain-dist/BUNDLE-INFO.txt records the exact bundled
 version. See debian/scripts/bundle-rust-toolchain.sh for the pinned version.

